Pieter wrote:
> My enterprising young Valkyrie, Elara(L8, neutral (ex)human valk), recently  
> fell through a trapdoor into a dead-end passage in the mines. With her pet 
> cat and pony. No way of digging or teleport, and a nice poly trap barring 
> the passage exit.
> 
> A couple steps later, we have:
> Elara, the Ogre King
> Topsy the Balrog (ex-pony)
> and Tora the Pit Fiend (ex-cat)
> 
> Is my only option to restore myself, to look for a source of polymorph and 
> poly control?

Not at all.  Ogre Kings aren't a bad form to be in, they can open doors 
normally, they eat.  Unless you start wearing an amulet of unchanging, 
you will revert to normal form on your own, or if your Orgeish HP get 
reduced to zero.

> 
> Just as importantly:
> Ive got two ridiculously powerful pets now. Do i use them, or flee in 
> abject terror? For sure, if either goes un-tame im gonna die horribly.
> On the other hand, these two can wipe the floor with a garrison of 
> soldiers, or snack on a passing dragon it seems. Expecially one they start 
> wielding some mean weapons?
> 
> Ive looked around a bit, but i see very little advice about how to use 
> greater demonoids as pets....

Well, Balrogs are verrry slow.  Even a slow character if he's careful 
can get in multiple attack rounds vs one.  Pit fiends I don't have any 
experience with.  (Demons are harder to acquire as pets, as it *takes* 
one to *charm* one)  But hey, if they wipe the floor with your enemies, 
then do use them for as long as they live.  They don't eat, so don't 
starve but don't gain tameness, either.  Just be careful with ranged 
attacks, and you'll be fine.  With their assistance, you'll soon be at a 
point in the game where balrogs and pit fiends merely tickle you, 
anyway.  At that point, they only have an upside.

Another way they could become hostile is if they are left too long on 
another level, but since they poly'ed from domestic form, they have 
quite a bit of tameness to burn through before you need worry about that.

